// @emit-error emitProgram: ref valtype with no interned shape
// THE SAME HOLE WITH NO GENERIC IN IT. An INLINE-SHAPE annotation carrying a `u8[]` field
// is interned by `internInlineShapeTy`, which — like `gaeEnsure` and for the same
// pass-order reason — declines QUIETLY on a field it cannot code. So this binding also
// reached `collectAnonShapes` with no row to match, and the literal's own syntax minted
// one: an i32-list field over the packed byte list, in a module that VALIDATED and ran.
//
// That is why the guard is not only in the generic-alias interner. `anonFieldCode` now
// refuses outright for a value whose CONTEXT-resolved type is the packed byte list
// (`nodeRepTyIxOf`, the sidecar the emitter's rep resolvers key on — the literal's own
// naive type is `i32[]`, since a bare `[7]` never infers `u8[]`). A synthetic row must
// never claim a rep the annotation it stands in for does not have.
//
// The LOCAL spelling of this same binding already refused ("binding's inline-shape type has
// an unsupported field"); the GLOBAL one did not, which is the drift.
const b: { v: u8[] } = { v: [7] }
print(1)
